1. `stdio.h` – Used for input and output.
2. `unistd.h` – Provides the `sleep()` function.
3. `main()` – Starting point of a C program.
4. `while(1)` – Runs a loop continuously.
5. `i++` – Increases the value of a variable by one.
6. `printf()` – Displays output on the screen.
7. `sleep(1)` – Pauses program execution for one second.
8. `gcc` – Compiles a C program.
9. `&` – Runs a program in the background.
10. `top` – Displays running processes and their CPU and memory usage.
11. `top -u username` – Displays processes of a particular user.
12. `top -p PID` – Displays a specific process.
13. `top -d 1` – Refreshes process information every one second.
14. `PID` – Identifies a running process.
15. `%CPU` – Shows the CPU usage of a process.
16. `%MEM` – Shows the memory usage of a process.
17. `jobs` – Displays background jobs.
18. `kill` – Terminates a running process.
19. `q` – Exits the `top` command.
